Photo2Pet
=========

Photo2Pet's current implementation is original project work released under
the MIT License in LICENSE. It includes:
  - make_pet.py: a single-photo asset pipeline (flood-fill white cutout,
    narrow white gap cleanup, anchor inference, and Pillow-only bilinear
    warping)
  - external asset packs: the runtime can load any sprite/dance/expression
    set via --assets or config.json, so a pet is no longer tied to one
    character
  - the bundled generic demo mascot, expressions, sprites, and dance frames,
    drawn from basic shapes by tools/make_demo_assets.py
  - the desktop-pet runtime, local web generator, documentation, and tests

The project builds on the author's earlier MIT-licensed desktop-pet
prototype. Some early runtime ideas (sprite normalization and part-based
dance) were carried forward from that work. Its copyright notice is retained
here as required by the MIT License:

  Copyright (c) 2026

Bundled demo artwork:
  - The generic demo mascot, expressions, sprites, and dance frames are drawn
    from basic shapes by tools/make_demo_assets.py. They are original project
    artwork and are distributed under the MIT License in LICENSE.
  - The project does not bundle third-party character or franchise artwork.
    User-provided photos and generated asset packs remain the user's
    responsibility and are not uploaded by the local tools.

Third-party components:
  - PySide6 / Qt / Shiboken6 (LGPLv3) - Qt for Python; Qt source code is
    available from https://code.qt.io/cgit/qt/ and PySide6 source from
    https://code.qt.io/cgit/pyside/pyside-setup.git
  - Python (PSF-2.0) - bundled runtime in the Windows executable
  - psutil (BSD-3-Clause)
  - nvidia-ml-py (BSD-3-Clause; imported as pynvml)
  - Pillow (MIT-CMU) - used by make_pet.py and the local web generator
  - PyInstaller (GPL-2.0-or-later with bootloader exception) - build tool;
    the bootloader is embedded in the Windows executable
  - rembg (MIT) - optional, only for non-white backgrounds; not bundled

The copyright notice above is retained as required by the MIT License. When
